            {
              "path": "docs/audit/2026-10-08/full-game/AC5_EXACT_ACCEPTANCE_05_RECEIPT.json",
              "bytes": 7471,
              "sha256": "5590d1b66ed59287069835ea19e9ffc3d52ea32a6166a9d0645757c7202885a9",
              "frozenCopy": "docs/audit/2026-10-08/full-game/accelerated-review-01/sources/docs/audit/2026-10-08/full-game/AC5_EXACT_ACCEPTANCE_05_RECEIPT.json"
            }
          ]
        },
        "scope": "Original regular markers and elapsed time",
        "currentAuthoritativeSource": {
          "path": "DescentReviewChanges/ReviewBible/docs/mechanics/COMBAT_ACTION_PLAYTEST.md",
          "bytes": 30409,
          "sha256": "f90d039142145fbd31c37992ebece70d7926dc4b6081e340f9a2fd9dc7237bc6",
          "frozenCopy": "docs/audit/2026-10-08/full-game/accelerated-review-01/sources/DescentReviewChanges/ReviewBible/docs/mechanics/COMBAT_ACTION_PLAYTEST.md",
          "heading": "## Time and event ordering — NEW",
          "line": 45
        },
        "exactAuthority": "## Time and event ordering — NEW\n\nFor a duration created in initiative, record the relevant original regular start/end marker. Existing effects keep that **virtual marker**, repeating every six seconds if the creature leaves or changes initiative. Reordering, rerolling, extra turns, death/removal or leaving/reentering initiative never restart an existing duration. New effects use the current schedule. Source death still ends concentration, a source-dependent aura/tether or an effect explicitly ending on death.\n\n- A bare hostile target-bound **N rounds** ends at the Nth future regular target-end marker. An in-progress target turn's current end does not count.\n- A bare self/source buff, ally-targeted buff or source-controlled aura **N rounds** ends at the Nth future source-start marker. Explicit target-turn, pulse or absolute timing overrides this default. Activation during source turn 1 for three rounds ends at source turn 4's start.\n- **Next turn** means the next future regular turn of the named creature, not the current turn's still-upcoming end. An unqualified next turn refers to source/user under the existing shared rule. Explicit “this turn” can include the current turn.\n- An outside-initiative bare N-round effect instead gets an absolute application-time + N×6 seconds deadline. Entering initiative preserves that deadline.\n- Explicit periodic profiles retain their registered clocks and tick counts. Never create a second timer merely because a generic duration rule also exists.\n\nThe [exact GPT review](../../../../docs/audit/2026-10-08/full-game/GPT_COMBAT_EXACT_FINDINGS.md) confirms ally-buff source clocks and excluding the current turn for explicit next-turn endpoints. The helper excludes a specific current-end marker only if that marker would otherwise be selected: application during a turn at time1 with end3 excludes3 and selects9; application at/after3 also selects9, without erroneously skipping again to15.\n\nAt a regular turn's **start**, resolve in this order:\n\n1. Expire start-ending effects and apply immediate state changes from those expirations.\n2. Refresh Reaction; tick regular-start recharge/non-action clocks.\n3. Resolve already-due absolute state recovery if now legal, including a previously blocked Stable recovery deadline.\n4. If still alive, dying and at 0 HP with death saves, make that turn's death save.\n5. Resolve other start effects and periodic events in application order.\n6. Begin voluntary turn decisions.\n\nAt **end**, resolve triggered effects, due damage, saves and maintenance before end-ending effects expire; then the slot finishes. No extra turn creates another regular marker. The caller must not reuse a resolved marker.\n\nFor simultaneous effects, earlier application timestamp precedes later. For simultaneous components of one source, its printed internal order controls; otherwise use stable application sequence, with source/mechanical ID as a final tie-break. Record that sequence when creating the effects. Beneficial/harmful labels do not change priority. Periodic family arbitration happens once per family/marker before its damage, retaining the family registry's consumed loser ticks.\n\nExamples: dying at 0 rolls its death save before ordinary start-turn healing; a fatal death save is not undone by ordinary healing. Stable at 0 skips the save, then start-turn damage can break Stable. A natural 20 can restore 1 HP before a due Bleed drops it to 0 as a new drop event. If Decay expires while a Stable recovery deadline is already due, the old deadline resolves once without rerolling recovery time.\n\n",
        "authoritySha256": "2e73bc43c564aef53495aa0166357d7691cd82adff13741f8e21c1939ba0e738",
        "trigger": "A timed event or expiry becomes due",
        "inputs": "Regular schedule, original marker, phase, extra-turn status",
        "outputs": "Ordered due events without duplicate ticks",
        "lifecycle": "Preserve original markers through reorder/absence",
        "exceptions": "Exact source-specific typed event order remains scoped",
        "knownSourceSpecificExtensions": [],
        "usedBy": [
          "AC4",
          "AC5"
        ],
        "usageCoverage": "Explicit known users, not a claim of exhaustive reverse-dependency indexing.",
        "reusableWithinScope": true,
        "summaryAuthority": "The exactAuthority and named source control; normalized fields index them and create no rules.",
