          "pointer": "/sharedRules/P20-SUPPRESSION-01"
        },
        "exactAuthority": "Reuse the exact actual suppressor/removal source. Lesser Antimagic, rank limits and source versus expression tests keep their accepted scope. AC6 Globe is not general antimagic: its fixed boundary blocks only its actual incoming rank-0–5 source cases, does not ban all internal casting, and does not erase an already attached buff merely because a creature enters. A fixed external ongoing field and a target-attached rider have different origin facts. A spell object is not a creature; physical Inferno fuel/rubble after actual creation is not a sustained magical field. No suppression pauses a deadline or restores a destroyed body, cleared crystal patch, spent shot or old command.",
        "authoritySha256": "21a681ecf8a27f94c3940fecf553489fb6d969cb1e4e31fb34a2d4763ef251c0",
        "trigger": "Only the accepted source-defined trigger, including actual lifecycle and eligibility.",
        "inputs": "Actual source/class access, paid resources, finite timing, body geometry and hidden/public state as specified in full model.",
        "outputs": "Only the exact named spell effects, state transitions and qualified damage-root records.",
        "lifecycle": "Original identity, clocks, consumed opportunities, source-specific suppression/ending and cleanup persist.",
        "exceptions": "No generic environment, healing, root, Fate presentation or spell-family promotion. Existing conditional source comparisons retain their limits.",
