        "operational": {
          "id": "fear",
          "activation": "Action",
          "rangeFeet": 30,
          "targets": "A 30-foot cone originating from you. At resolution snapshot every creature in the cone with line of effect from you, including allies and yourself if physically within the actual area; no selective omission or individual-perception requirement. No additional hearing, gaze or visual-eligibility gate.",
          "duration": "Concentration, up to one minute. In initiative, the maximum ends at the caster's tenth future regular-turn START after application, excluding any start already underway/passed. If begun outside initiative, the maximum is 60 elapsed seconds. Preserve the original virtual marker/absolute deadline through initiative changes, extra turns, absence and planar travel; no timing-mode change resets it.",
          "concentration": true,
          "components": [
            "V",
            "S",
            "F"
          ],
          "resolution": "Use actual rank-3/5-RP class access: Enchantment for Bard, Crimson Agent, Mirrorsage, Thief, Wizard or Paladin; Illusion for Monk at its preserved level. Each eligible creature independently makes a Wisdom save. Success: no effect. Failure applies actual Frightened toward you under its own actual defenses. No repeat save is added.",
          "effect": "Actual Frightened gives disadvantage on ability checks and attacks while its fear source is visible/in line of sight and prevents willingly moving closer to that source. The initial cone determines the fixed target set only: leaving it, increasing distance or later loss of sight does not end the application. No forced flight, Dash, dropped items or extra Action restriction is added.",
          "scaling": "None. No automatic increase in range, targets, duration, magnitude or uses.",
          "limitations": "Concentration loss, expiry and actual removal end the relevant application. Calm Emotions suppresses its Frightened mechanical effects while source records, concentration and clocks continue; resumption does not reset duration or reapply one-time events. No damage-ending clause, ongoing range tether or new hard-control claim. Independent Fear applications keep their own source relationships and concentration/deadlines without stacked numerical penalties. Both modes preserve their actual school; accessing one does not grant the other. With no repeat save, outside initiative needs only the original absolute duration clock. Actual class access/repertoire, legal action/components/RP, concentration transitions, Dissonance/Refrain and paid cast/counter order follow SPELL_INTEGRATION_RULES.md. A legal cast pays before hidden eligibility/effect resolution; failure or countering refunds nothing and restores no displaced concentration. V is audible, S needs the ordinary usable hand, and F is the normal class focus. Saves use the actual casting class's spell DC and binary-save rules. Hidden eligibility supplies no free diagnostic. Creature type alone supplies no mental immunity; Charmed-only immunity has only its actual condition scope. No generic upcast, extra action budget or resource generation.",
          "designNotes": "PRESERVED: both schools/rank-3 access, Action, 30-foot cone, V/S/F, WIS, actual Frightened and concentration minute. NEW: all-creature initial snapshot, caster fear-source relation, explicit no-repeat-save/no-extra-sensory-gate procedure and no ongoing cone tether. No unrelated-system forced flight/drop rules are imported.",
          "implementationStatus": "REVIEWED authored operational PLAYTEST manuscript; runtime, human balance and broader integration pending",
          "sourcePlacements": [
            {
              "name": "Fear",
              "school": "Enchantment",
              "level": 3,
              "summary": "Creatures in 30-ft cone must make WIS save or become frightened."
