        },
        "procedure": "KEEP Action, 60 feet, V/S/F, one target, 4d6 psychic per round and WIS ending saves. Preserve Core Instantaneous as a metadata conflict. NEW one perceived creature with line of effect makes initial WIS; success establishes nothing and deals no damage. Failure establishes a private mental nightmare with an independently real magical psychic-damage component, concentration up to 60 elapsed seconds. Ordinary blindness/deafness is not immunity to a mental nightmare. No Frightened, Stunned, paralysis, compulsory movement or Action loss is imported from either lower Phantasmal Killer placement; no hard-control claim is made for damage alone.\n\nOn failed initial admission, deal 4d6 psychic immediately only if this named spell family's exposure for that target in the actual numbered round is unused. At each subsequent actual regular target START after mandatory start processing, an operative application attempts the same packet. Across every Greater Phantasmal Killer caster/application on that recipient, allow at most one packet per numbered round, including initial packets; select the earliest active eligible application, with neutral source/application order for ties. Record the opportunity before resolving its damage, so immunity or an HP floor does not permit another source to retry that exposure. A wholly suppressed application cannot supply a packet; its scheduled opportunity is lost, not banked. Recasting does not clear that target's family history. The lower Phantasmal Killer is a different named source with its own preserved 4d10 clauses and caps; no silent numerical upgrade, downgrade or cross-family merger is proposed.\n\nThe target repeats WIS at every affected actual regular END, including the upcoming END of a turn already underway. Success ends only the corresponding application before any later packet, with no additional damage attached to that successful save. Separate applications have separate ending saves and concentration, even though their damage shares the family exposure cap. Outside initiative there is the eligible immediate application packet, then future START-type packet opportunities every six seconds after application and END-only saves on the same six-second boundaries, resolving packet before ending save when both are due. On entering initiative map the first unresolved packet/save to actual next regular START/END without an extra transition packet, preserving original expiry and spent family exposure. At the exact maximum deadline expiry wins.\n\nTrue Seeing or recognizing the nightmare identifies its false depiction but, by this explicit NEW separation, does not itself remove the independently sustained damaging spell. Actual protection against this mental illusion can prevent/suppress the whole application where its text says so; psychic immunity prevents only damage, while Fear immunity alone has no effect here. No mental image supplies the caster private memories, remote senses or the target's hidden location. The spell has no continuing range tether after establishment. Target death, actual removal, concentration ending or expiry ends its application. Suppression does not stop its clock or scheduled ending saves; no extra tick occurs on resumption. These choices preserve the lower printed 4d6 amount and deliberately place its comparison with lower-rank 4d10 in the joint issue register.",
        "previousFullProposalUnchanged": {
          "spellId": "greater-phantasmal-killer",
          "procedure": "KEEP Action, 60 feet, V/S/F, one target, 4d6 psychic per round and WIS ending saves. Preserve Core Instantaneous as a metadata conflict. NEW one perceived creature with line of effect makes initial WIS; success establishes nothing and deals no damage. Failure establishes a private mental nightmare with an independently real magical psychic-damage component, concentration up to 60 elapsed seconds. Ordinary blindness/deafness is not immunity to a mental nightmare. No Frightened, Stunned, paralysis, compulsory movement or Action loss is imported from either lower Phantasmal Killer placement; no hard-control claim is made for damage alone.\n\nOn failed initial admission, deal 4d6 psychic immediately only if this named spell family's exposure for that target in the actual numbered round is unused. At each subsequent actual regular target START after mandatory start processing, an operative application attempts the same packet. Across every Greater Phantasmal Killer caster/application on that recipient, allow at most one packet per numbered round, including initial packets; select the earliest active eligible application, with neutral source/application order for ties. Record the opportunity before resolving its damage, so immunity or an HP floor does not permit another source to retry that exposure. A wholly suppressed application cannot supply a packet; its scheduled opportunity is lost, not banked. Recasting does not clear that target's family history. The lower Phantasmal Killer is a different named source with its own preserved 4d10 clauses and caps; no silent numerical upgrade, downgrade or cross-family merger is proposed.\n\nThe target repeats WIS at every affected actual regular END, including the upcoming END of a turn already underway. Success ends only the corresponding application before any later packet, with no additional damage attached to that successful save. Separate applications have separate ending saves and concentration, even though their damage shares the family exposure cap. Outside initiative there is the eligible immediate application packet, then future START-type packet opportunities every six seconds after application and END-only saves on the same six-second boundaries, resolving packet before ending save when both are due. On entering initiative map the first unresolved packet/save to actual next regular START/END without an extra transition packet, preserving original expiry and spent family exposure. At the exact maximum deadline expiry wins.\n\nTrue Seeing or recognizing the nightmare identifies its false depiction but, by this explicit NEW separation, does not itself remove the independently sustained damaging spell. Actual protection against this mental illusion can prevent/suppress the whole application where its text says so; psychic immunity prevents only damage, while Fear immunity alone has no effect here. No mental image supplies the caster private memories, remote senses or the target's hidden location. The spell has no continuing range tether after establishment. Target death, actual removal, concentration ending or expiry ends its application. Suppression does not stop its clock or scheduled ending saves; no extra tick occurs on resumption. These choices preserve the lower printed 4d6 amount and deliberately place its comparison with lower-rank 4d10 in the joint issue register.",
          "workedCases": [
            "IN6-02-A: The target fails initial WIS and receives a rolled 15 psychic damage before its defenses. A later target START in that same numbered round produces no second packet. At its affected END it succeeds on WIS and ends that application; success itself causes no damage. The caster spent 13 RP and receives no refund because only one packet occurred.",
            "IN6-02-B: Two casters maintain admitted Greater Phantasmal Killer records on one target. Only the earliest eligible record supplies that round's 4d6 opportunity; the target still resolves each application's own ending save. Psychic immunity can reduce the actual damage to zero without reopening the opportunity. Identifying the nightmare supplies no automatic dispel under this proposed independent-damage rule."
          ],
          "newChoices": "NEW initial WIS, concentration minute, exact initial/START/END timing and shared named-family exposure; no imported fear rider; explicit preservation of 4d6 despite the lower spell's 4d10.",
          "questionId": "IN6-02",
          "originalQuestion": "Preserve4d6 PSYCHIC PER ROUND with WIS SAVE ENDING,Core Action/60ft/Instantaneous. Resolve finite lifetime/concentration and initial-save versus first-damage timing. Bind every later4d6 packet to one stated turn/round event and give exact repeated-save timing,damage on successful initial/repeat saves and ending on caster/target loss. Compare both lower Phantasmal Killer placements without automatically importing their fear rider,damage or durations. Define who perceives the illusion, whether fear immunity stops a separate psychic component, actual hard-control admission only if such a component is added, and no extra hit from entering initiative or recasting the same source. Instantaneous metadata must remain preserved as a conflict,not silently edited away.",
