          "sourceRecordSha256": "32c138b79f79636b2ae9991a504b647c2c1b7b724561d02bbe5598a8084714a8",
          "status": "unadopted-unsent-operating-proposal",
          "examplesAreRuntimeTests": false
        },
        "previousSharedProposalUnchanged": {
          "status": "UNADOPTED AND UNSENT. Thirteen complete mechanical proposals and twenty-six examples await actual GPT discussion and exact review. NEW identifies explicit design additions. No ordinary spell, class grant, bestiary profile, runtime or cosmology is approved by this document.",
          "casting": "Retain every actual rank-six/base 13 RP class access row and school: Illusion ordinarily Wizard 11, Bard/Mirrorsage 16, Crimson Agent 19; Necromancy Cleric/Druid/Wizard 11, Shaman 16, Crimson Agent 19. True Seeing retains its separate actual Divination/Illusion rows. All retain Action, range 60 feet and V/S/F except Invisible Tide range 30 feet and Blood Fog/Circle of Death V/S/M-or-F. For those two use the existing unpriced ordinary material/focus alternative, without inventing a consumed reagent or price. Actual repertoire, source ability, components, RP modifiers, Dissonance/Refrain, concentration transitions and interrupt rules apply. A legal cast commits before hidden eligibility and its counter window. No failed-cast refund, automatic upcast or level scaling. DC is 8 + actual PB + actual class modifier; spell attack is PB + that modifier. Binary spell saves remain distinct from four-degree ability tasks.",
          "geometry": "Declare modes, legal perceived centers and named targets before hidden resolution. Caster-to-center/target line of effect is required; areas also require center-to-recipient line of effect. An indiscriminate area does not require separately seeing each recipient and includes allies/self unless its card says otherwise. Fixed spheres have their stated three-dimensional radii, not diameter or distance from the caster. Opaque physical barriers remain real. A subjective enemy predicate uses the caster's actual existing knowledge and hostility toward that creature, not secret alignment, allegiance or an extra detection sense. An already-known enemy can be affected while currently unseen; an entirely unknown creature is not automatically classified as hostile by this spell.",
          "clocks": "NEW cohort bindings: one minute is 60 elapsed seconds from resolution. Expiry wins at its exact deadline. Regular START/END means the actual ordinary turn, never an extra turn. END-only ending saves include a current regular turn's upcoming END; outside initiative they occur every six seconds after application and the first unresolved opportunity maps to the next actual regular END on entering initiative. Original deadlines and spent events persist through initiative changes, absence and suppression. A companion-only recipient uses its actual original-owner regular attached phase START/END for an expressly assigned spell tick/save, without generating a regular turn, refresh or death save; if that phase is absent use the original six-second spell-only schedule. This NEW bridge supplies only the card's due effect/save, never a companion Action. Compelled movement uses only a real available movement phase. Suppressed opportunities are lost, not queued; resumption grants no immediate periodic packet.",
          "illusions": "Use the current LR-G07 procedure for a sensory image: a personally accessible relevant sense and an Action permit INT (Investigation) against the original spell DC, with Core task degrees/natural shifts. Success/Critical Success identifies that illusion for that observer. A failed investigation needs genuinely new evidence or method before retry. Conclusive personally witnessed physical contradiction reveals the contradicted false content; a warning alone does not globally reveal it. Informed observers perceive through the identified false sensory overlay using their actual senses. No image creates physical cover, support, material, creature HP, inventory, remote senses, knowledge or an Action unless explicitly authored below. A damaging magical component can remain after its sensory depiction is identified when the specific proposal expressly separates them. This last distinction and True Seeing interfaces require joint agreement.",
          "damageAndControl": "Apply actual typed defenses, damage sharing, temporary HP, HP prevention/floors, Instant Death, Wounds, concentration and death in their reviewed order. actualDamageDealt is real temporary HP absorbed plus ordinary HP lost, excluding overkill and duplicate parent/child transfer amounts. Ordinary healing keeps current maximum, Critical ceiling, modifiers and prohibitions. Claim the combined source-character/target/encounter hard-control allowance only on actual establishment of a whole-Action/turn component; no refund on ending/replacement/suppression. No postponed application or invented fallback when initial admission fails. Actual component immunities retain their scope: Fear-only immunity is not universal mental immunity, and creature type alone supplies none. Compelled conduct uses existing safe-route/resource/secret/oath restrictions and Compelled Budget Arbitration: earliest real instruction, one actual budget, compatible demands share one execution.",
          "createdCompanions": "For the newly created Wraith and Undead profiles, all owned assets share one Bonus Action command and one offensive companion Action per numbered round with every other companion/device. During the owner's regular turn, issue one simple mental order to one perceived body within 60 feet/line of effect; it supplies no sensory feed, language proficiency or unknown facts. Execute in the actual attached phase after the whole owner turn, not immediately at casting. A body has one profiled attack or a legal basic Action; no printed Multiattack, free Help engine, Reaction, Bonus Action, casting, class resource or autonomous offense is acquired. Uncommanded capable bodies move defensively and Dodge. Normal command failure has no refund. Original creating source owner supplies current spell attack and total PB for all six saves; ordinary ability checks use the stated ability modifiers, without proficiency. Genuinely source-qualified maximum-HP modifiers apply to the stated base HP. A transfer/control effect supplies no new profile or original-owner statistics. Command Undeath has its separately defined bridge for preexisting creatures.",
          "identity": "Keep actual physical body, source owner, controller, originating spell, current HP, inventory and all histories distinct. A conjured body provides no corpse, harvest or transferable intrinsic gear. A converted real corpse is consumed once and never becomes fresh raising/recipe fuel by destruction, release or renaming. Actual carried gear stays real and changes custody only through physical actions. No new resurrection permission, soul capture, afterlife destination, planar route or identity lore follows from a spell name. Mechanical creature type is not a decision about cosmology.",
          "workedBaseline": "Unless specified otherwise, an eligible Wizard 11 has current/maximum RP 40, INT +4, PB +4, spell attack +8, DC 16 and Dissonance 0/limit 10. One ordinary rank-six cast costs 13 RP, leaving 27, with its real first-cast cadence increment. Examples are authored adjudications, not runtime executions or balance approval."
        },
        "sourcePromise": "4d6amount preserved despite lower-rank4d10comparison; no impliedFrightened orhardguard.",
        "remainingDecisions": "Actual independent4d6component establishment/root vslower4d10; initialplusSTART family cap, eachsourceENDsave; TrueSeeing source dependency pending and no automatic cure; current exactdigital clocks/visibility, classaccess.",
        "damageRootProposal": {
          "spellId": "greater-phantasmal-killer",
          "status": "NEW source-specific proposal, requires Director agreement",
          "components": [
            {
              "name": "independent recurring nightmare damage",
              "rootKind": "one recipient/application root",
              "dealer": "actual original caster character; no creature identity is created for a field, beam or object cannon",
              "creationCheckpoint": "When this source actually establishes its target-attached damage component; snapshot dealer then, even if a later cap consumes the first scheduled opportunity without damage.",
              "descendants": "All expressly scheduled packets of that application retain its original flag. Suppression, immunity, healing, initiative transition and later caster Veil changes do not refresh it; a genuinely new admitted replacement application creates a new root."
            }
          ],
          "reason": "Propose the same explicit establishment checkpoint as now-accepted lower Phantasmal Killer, retaining this separate source’s printed4d6 amount, no implied fear, class-school access and distinct schedule. Lower-source acceptance does not approve this extension; actual concurrence is still required."
        },
        "originalCaseIds": [
          "IN6-02-A",
          "IN6-02-B"
        ]
      },
      "completeSharedRules": {
        "P20-CASTING-01": "Reuse actual class-access/repertoire, paid costs, component, concentration and Dissonance/Refrain procedures from the exact registry. None of these drafts grants a new class row, rank, upcast or resource maximum. A continuous field, stored rider or command does not itself cast again. Actual target/caster predicates are rechecked at the source-defined checkpoint, without refund or diagnostic disclosure from hidden failure.",
        "P20-DIGITAL-GEOMETRY-01": "NEW bounded clarification for these 20 proposals: measure the actual occupied body against the continuous authored volume/surface, with actual cover/line of effect. Five-foot lengths remain real lengths, not a rounding of positions onto tabletop squares. Source-authored five-foot destructible/fuel partitions remain fixed object identities; changing path sampling, zoom or visual mesh subdivision cannot create more targets, HP or exposure. Evaluate a genuine entry at the first boundary crossing/contact, resolve it once before continuing the same trajectory, and preserve actual remaining movement. Teleport crosses no intermediate path; an arrival can trigger only a source explicitly authorizing arrival. Snapshot simultaneous recipients once before their consequences; destroyed cover creates no second wave.",
        "P20-CLOCKS-01": "NEW explicit cohort bindings: absolute field deadlines are resolution+60 seconds where the procedure states one minute; expiry wins at equality. Source-owned pulses at resolution and +6 through +54 do not require a caster turn or grant a creature turn. A finite target/source marker schedule records its original regular markers at creation under accepted time ordering; reorder, extra turns and departure preserve the original virtual schedule, six seconds apart. Explicit future-turn endpoints exclude an in-progress turn/phase; an ending save expressly including current END keeps that exception. At START, apply accepted expiry/recovery/death-save ordering before periodic damage. At END, due damage/eligible ending saves precede that source endpoint cleanup, except a card explicitly expires before its redundant last save. Suppression consumes a due scheduled opportunity with no damage or catch-up. Ended creature identities have no recipient; administrative deadline bookkeeping never resurrects one.",
        "P20-ATTACHED-PHASE-01": "NEW source-specific bridge for the target-clock proposals in this cohort, not a general companion turn: an owner-attached recipient uses the original owner regular attached-phase beginning/end only for the stated spell packet or ending save. A future phase excludes one already underway. If no such real phase exists, retain a six-second spell-only checkpoint and finite original endpoint. This checkpoint supplies only a due packet/save or expiry that the spell actually grants; it supplies no Action, movement, Bonus Action, Reaction refresh, recharge, or ordinary death save. Source-required real Action/command maintenance cannot execute at an administrative checkpoint. Root identity, prior spent exposures, endpoint and finite tick count survive controller or schedule changes.",
        "P20-FAMILY-EXPOSURE-01": "NEW per-source anti-duplication applies only where the individual procedure names a family cap: record target identity, named spell family, explicit category and numbered round. Different owners/casts share that named ledger; distinct spell names and explicitly separate Wall of Fire categories do not merge. Outside initiative use the scene continuing six-second exposure cycle, fixed before the relevant exposure. Preserve its spent state through a transition to the current combat round until that mapped interval ends; never refresh just by changing timing mode. Immunity/save/prevention after actual admission still consumes the exposure; wholly suppressed or geometrically ineligible sources cannot claim it. Simultaneous eligible sources use established application order then stable identity. Immolation instead uses the already accepted ongoing-fire arbitration at each identical target marker.",
        "P20-DAMAGE-FUNDING-01": "Reuse actual typed defenses, temporary HP, HP floors, Wounds, concentration, death/Null life order and one original recipient event. No inferred damage amount from structural failure or overkill. ActualDamageDealt remains real tempHP absorption plus normal HP loss. Healing/funding is a separate consumer: first exclude any terminal branch whose actual transfer/source flag forbids derived healing or recovery, then apply the spell-specific donor predicate, sum eligible branches once and floor the half once. Never count a split parent again. Burden Shared and Life Linked restrictions remain operative; a numeric branch amount alone is not funding permission. Preserve the distinct pending Leeching Plague donor exclusions and Enervation wider proposal for explicit Director disposition.",
        "P20-RNG-INFORMATION-01": "Authored dice are engine RNG. Original component identity, draw method, save factor and cached ordinal value remain private engine state unless an actual separately accepted presentation policy grants the exact disclosure. This candidate grants no new public dice viewer, hidden-target list, successful-save feedback, enemy-identity scan or Fate eligibility. Shared damage dice do not merge recipient roots. The accepted exact DE4 five-entry presentation policy applies only where its actual source predicates pass; it does not automatically disclose any private periodic, delayed, penalty or random-selection operation in this cohort. An actual qualifying OVERT-ATTACK d20 can use that entry without exposing a hidden Synaptic Static d6, hidden modifier cause or later damage pool. No sixth presentation entry is proposed here. No RNG seed or future draw is exposed. If a source has no admitted recipient and no explicit source-authored event-generation rule, do not invent a damage event merely to publish a roll.",
        "P20-ROOT-01": "Every damage source uses its explicit pending per-source mapping in damageRootProposals. These are NEW decisions requiring concurrence; accepted Forbiddance/Chain Arc/Skybrand and lower nightmare rules do not silently generalize. Root creation alone spends no Action, deals no damage, triggers no Wound, generates no material, and grants no hidden information. Pure transfer retains flags; an attached component can retain an old flag while a genuinely new operated attack creates its own root. Physical fire and Sonic debris mappings are bounded to the exact finite proposed outputs.",
        "P20-SUPPRESSION-01": "Reuse the exact actual suppressor/removal source. Lesser Antimagic, rank limits and source versus expression tests keep their accepted scope. AC6 Globe is not general antimagic: its fixed boundary blocks only its actual incoming rank-0–5 source cases, does not ban all internal casting, and does not erase an already attached buff merely because a creature enters. A fixed external ongoing field and a target-attached rider have different origin facts. A spell object is not a creature; physical Inferno fuel/rubble after actual creation is not a sustained magical field. No suppression pauses a deadline or restores a destroyed body, cleared crystal patch, spent shot or old command."
      },
