        },
        "originalQuestion": "Preserve forcing a creature to move in a chosen direction, WIS negates, Action/60ft/Instantaneous. Define when the movement occurs, finite distance or ordinary movement budget, what the direction anchors to, known safe/legal paths and blocked-route behavior. Decide whether it spends the target movement and provokes opportunity attacks, or is an explicit displacement; do not blend both models opportunistically. Resolve voluntary/forced transport, movement modes/support, hazards and actual absolute restrictions, current versus future turn timing, and the shared compelled-budget priority. No unprinted Dash, Action denial, extra movement, repeated off-turn movement or permission to spend optional resources.",
        "historicalProposalUnchanged": {
          "spellId": "compulsion",
          "procedureScope": "complete-proposed-mechanical-spell",
          "procedure": "Action; range 60 feet; V/S/F. One perceived creature with line of effect makes WIS. Success does nothing. NEW: on failure record one fixed world-space direction chosen at casting, not a homing target, and one pending movement instruction for the next future regular turn, excluding a turn already underway. At that START after normal processing and before voluntary movement, spend up to 30 feet of the target’s actual remaining ordinary movement moving as far as reasonably possible in that direction along a legal known route. The target/controller selects the safest legal route; use only its actual available movement modes, support and distances. No knowingly self-destructive route, unsupported step, prohibited transport or optional resource expenditure is compelled. Ordinary opportunity attacks remain possible; this is compelled use of movement, not push/pull displacement. No Dash, Action loss, extra movement, teleport permission or new speed is supplied. A blocked route or Speed 0 permits only the actual safe meaningful movement available, possibly none; no alternative direction or banked retry follows. The instruction competes through existing compelled-budget arbitration with priority at establishment. It expires after this opportunity. Outside initiative resolve one ordinary movement opportunity within six elapsed seconds; establish initiative first when combat timing matters. A companion uses only movement in its next actual original-owner regular attached phase, with no extra phase, Action, offensive allowance or owner resource charge. NEW: one pending application per caster/target; a later actually established application replaces that caster’s prior one. Other casters’ instructions retain distinct histories but cannot reset the same movement budget. Suppression at the execution opportunity prevents execution without deferring it.",
          "newChoices": "NEW: fixed direction, one future movement opportunity capped at 30 feet within actual remaining movement, no Action denial, explicit single-use/companion timing and replacement.",
          "workedCases": [
            "A creature with 20 feet of remaining movement can be compelled to use at most those 20 feet, not an extra 30.",
            "A known lethal drop blocks that route. The spell grants neither hovering nor a substitute teleport, and does not wait indefinitely for a path to open."
          ],
          "questionId": "DE4-12",
          "originalQuestion": "Preserve forcing a creature to move in a chosen direction, WIS negates, Action/60ft/Instantaneous. Define when the movement occurs, finite distance or ordinary movement budget, what the direction anchors to, known safe/legal paths and blocked-route behavior. Decide whether it spends the target movement and provokes opportunity attacks, or is an explicit displacement; do not blend both models opportunistically. Resolve voluntary/forced transport, movement modes/support, hazards and actual absolute restrictions, current versus future turn timing, and the shared compelled-budget priority. No unprinted Dash, Action denial, extra movement, repeated off-turn movement or permission to spend optional resources.",
