        },
        "historicalQuestion": "Preserve ending MULTIPLE magical effects in30ft RADIUS, Core Action/range30ft/Instantaneous. Separate point-targeting range from area and define complete finite candidates,sight/line of effect,perception or hidden-effect handling,target choice and maximum or all-effect scope explicitly. Supply source-bound dispel rank/DC/check/outcomes rather than borrowing a familiar game. Determine one roll versus separate rolls,order,whole parent versus one recipient/rider and how an ended barrier affects the initial area snapshot. Compare reviewed Dispel Magic,Dispel Resonance and lesser variants. Do not silently reduce multiple to one, suppress instead of end,delete magic items,undo completed healing/costs/material transformations or reveal protected effects through a free success report. Actual magical sources and separately governed exceptions control eligibility.",
        "historicalProposalEvidence": {
          "spellId": "greater-dispel",
          "procedure": "KEEP Action,casting-point range30feet,30-foot RADIUS and ending multiple magical effects. NEW choose one perceived center within30feet. At resolution capture every ongoing independently addressable spell-effect application with some actual affected body, discrete effect/anchor or freestanding area portion inside the30-foot sphere and center line of effect, allies included. No numerical cap and no selective omission after hidden results; individual effect perception is not required for this area purge, a NEW distinction from the reviewed single-target lower dispels. Hidden actual source data determines eligibility without identifying magic to the caster. Exclude instantaneous completed consequences, innate nonmagical traits, class engines as a whole, permanent magic-item enchantments/body, and expressly nondispellable effects. A nonspell magical component is eligible only when its own actual source explicitly supplies a dispel interface/rank or DC; no guessed rank0 is assigned. For an eligible ordinary spell application of recorded original generating rank0through5, end it automatically. For rank6through9, make one source spellcasting-ability+PB task check per original generating cast at DC10+twice that recorded rank; reuse that check for all captured recipient applications from that same cast. Apply the actual Core task degrees/natural shifts; Success/Critical Success ends each captured eligible application, Failure/Critical Failure ends none from that check, with no extra critical damage. Unknown actual rank without a separate supplied dispel interface is not guessed into eligibility. Same-cast multi-recipient records are individually captured: ending a buff on one recipient does not automatically remove unselected remote recipients or the caster's concentration unless the source's real parent dependency requires it. For a genuinely indivisible wall/field, a reachable intersecting portion selects that one effect, so successful dispelling ends the whole indivisible effect with its ordinary consequences. A selected created summon follows its actual independent-body versus whole-cohort ending procedure, not a fabricated corpse or magic-item destruction rule. A spell-generated ongoing curse can qualify if within this scope and not specially protected; a disease now persisting without an ongoing spell and a curse requiring an explicit special cure do not acquire a dispel permission. Process captured applications by stable original-cast/application identity; shared checks are rolled once when needed, and a source already ended by an earlier real dependency needs no duplicate roll or ending. The original capture does not expand when a dispelled wall ceases to block center line of effect. An effect that appears later during resolution was not captured. Eligible suppressed but still-present records may be ended if the actual dispel can reach them; the field suppressing this new cast still prevents it where applicable. No countering a pending cast, undoing HP/costs, reclaiming consumed ingredients, erasing permanent ordinary matter, catalog spell removal or diagnostic success report follows. Source endings can have their ordinary visible outcomes, from which observers may infer normally.",
          "newChoices": "NEW indiscriminate finite area snapshot, automatic original rank≤5 and one shared higher-rank task check per generating cast at10+2rank; actual application versus indivisible-field ending and no snapshot expansion. Rank/interface exclusions stay explicit.",
          "workedCases": [
            "AB5-03-A: The snapshot includes a rank2buff, rank5field and two recipient records from one rank6cast. The first two end automatically. Wizard+8rolls15for23against rank6DC22, so both captured rank6recipient applications end using that one success. An unselected remote recipient remains unless the original source truly binds it to the ended parent.",
            "AB5-03-B: An eligible wall blocks another effect when the purge snapshot is taken. Ending that wall does not add the formerly hidden effect to this cast. A rank6check rolling natural20+0against22 uses the reviewed natural improvement from Failure to Success; no standard-game flat natural20 rule or free protected-effect identification is substituted."
          ],
          "questionId": "AB5-03",
          "originalQuestion": "Preserve ending MULTIPLE magical effects in30ft RADIUS, Core Action/range30ft/Instantaneous. Separate point-targeting range from area and define complete finite candidates,sight/line of effect,perception or hidden-effect handling,target choice and maximum or all-effect scope explicitly. Supply source-bound dispel rank/DC/check/outcomes rather than borrowing a familiar game. Determine one roll versus separate rolls,order,whole parent versus one recipient/rider and how an ended barrier affects the initial area snapshot. Compare reviewed Dispel Magic,Dispel Resonance and lesser variants. Do not silently reduce multiple to one, suppress instead of end,delete magic items,undo completed healing/costs/material transformations or reveal protected effects through a free success report. Actual magical sources and separately governed exceptions control eligibility.",
