          "sourceRecordSha256": "7fcb0f210b9523bb351df7f0203d139f907681edab47ee7cc153d0673f600728",
          "status": "unadopted-unsent-operating-proposal",
          "examplesAreRuntimeTests": false
        },
        "procedure": "Action; casting-point range 30 feet; V/S/F; base 10 RP; Instantaneous. Choose one perceived center within 30 feet. At resolution take one immutable snapshot of every ongoing independently addressable magical effect application having an affected body, discrete anchor/object effect, or freestanding area portion inside the 30-foot-radius sphere and center line of effect. Allies are included. Individual effect perception is not required; no numerical cap or selective post-result omission exists.\n\nEligible ordinary spell applications retain their original generating rank. Rank 0-5 ends automatically. Rank 6-9 requires one check per original generating cast using the caster's actual spellcasting ability + PB against DC 10 + 2×recorded rank. Reuse that one roll for all captured applications from the same generating cast. Apply current Core task degrees/natural shifts. A nonspell magical component is eligible only if its own source explicitly supplies a dispel interface/rank/DC; never assign rank 0 by appearance or RP cost.\n\nCapture is fixed before any endings. If a captured Wall of Force ends and reveals another effect behind it, that effect is not added. A captured indivisible wall/field ends as one effect on successful/automatic dispel; recipient-specific applications from one cast end only where captured unless their real parent dependency says ending one ends all. Suppressed-but-still-existing records can be dispelled if this cast itself can reach them. Completed instantaneous consequences, permanent matter, class engines, permanent item enchantments and explicitly nondispellable effects are outside scope.\n\nThis is distinct from Wizard class Dispel Magic `/cards/19`: that class spell costs 3 RP, range 60, Recharge 2, auto through rank 3, and uses INT+PB vs DC 10+rank above 3. Sigil Authority `/cards/22` names Counterspell and Dispel Magic only and does not modify Greater Dispel. Xi remains its own consent-based branch-ending source and grants no Greater Dispel permission.",
        "newScopedAuthorship": [
          "Immutable 30-ft area snapshot",
          "rank0-5 automatic; rank6-9 one shared check per generating cast at DC10+2rank",
          "nonspell only with explicit dispel interface",
          "no snapshot expansion",
          "class Dispel/Sigil Authority kept distinct"
        ],
        "currentInterfaces": [
          "Wizard /cards/19 Dispel Magic",
          "Wizard /cards/22 Sigil Authority",
          "Xi remains separate"
        ],
        "profile": null,
        "sourceConflicts": [],
