        "procedure": "Action; range 60 feet; V/S/F. One perceived creature with line of effect makes WIS. Success establishes nothing. KEEP failure loses one round in confusion. NEW on a failed save, if actual defenses permit and the shared hard-control allowance is unused, establish a custom lost-round state immediately until the end of the target’s next future regular turn, excluding an in-progress turn. There is no concentration; this ongoing rank-4 rider expressly survives the original Instantaneous metadata and is subject to qualifying removal/suppression. It prohibits new full Actions, Bonus Actions, Reactions and voluntary movement commitments. Already legally committed Actions/Reactions finish their actual resolution; movement already spent is not refunded, while later uncommitted movement cannot begin. Extra turns inside the interval gain no exception and do not shorten the endpoint. The target still makes actual required saves, death saves and ending checks, can perceive/think and use permitted speech, retains passive defenses and can be moved by independent forces. This is not Stunned, Incapacitated, Paralyzed, Blinded or the ordinary Confusion spell; it imposes no automatic failed saves, attack advantage, forced hostile attack or concentration loss by itself. Ordinary damage or a separately applicable incapacitating state still affects concentration normally. Apply the shared future attached-phase/six-second bridge where the recipient has no regular turn, without inventing a companion turn. Consume the source-character/target/encounter guard only on establishment; an already spent guard or relevant immunity blocks this entire lost-round state, with no replacement penalty. Charmed-only immunity does not cover a rider that imposes no Charmed condition; actual broader defenses apply. Suppression permits whatever normal actions are otherwise legal while suppressed, without restoring budgets already spent or extending the endpoint. The used hard-control allowance remains used after early removal or suppression. No repeat save is added; expiry/removal/death of the recipient ends the rider. No teleportation or stopped personal time occurs.",
        "selectedProcedureSource": {
