        "completeEarlierRecordUnchanged": {
          "spellId": "mass-mirage",
          "procedure": "Action; select up to six distinct perceived creatures within60feet and line of effect, including self; V/S/F. KEEP individual appearances as others including voice and silhouette. NEW one-hour nonconcentration lifetime instead of undefined instantaneous permanence. A willing recipient accepts; an unwilling one makes CHA, success preventing only its own shell. Choose each disguise independently before saves; no replacement target after a save. Use the shared real-body/visual-disbelief shell and actual recorded appearance. NEW voice overlay changes the recipient's own actual utterance to the chosen audible qualities/known imitation while it speaks; choose from voice samples actually heard by the caster, or a designed generic ordinary voice. It transmits only words/sounds the recipient genuinely produces and understands when understanding is required; no unknown passwords, language, memories, perfect authentication or supernatural voice power. A sampled individual can be imitated plausibly, but ordinary social verification/context and investigation still apply. No greater-than-normal shout volume, speech while unable to speak, replacement verbal spell component or bypass of Silence. A listener can use Action INT/Investigation vs original DC when actual vocal evidence creates uncertainty; success recognizes this voice overlay, not the recipient's undisclosed true identity. Silence/Deafened or visual-only illusion penetration affects only its actual sensory channel; voice recognition does not automatically supply an unseen real face. Each recipient can spend its own Action dismissing its shell; caster can spend an Action ending selected still-live shells without remote sensory information. One Mass Mirage shell per recipient across casters; a newly accepted/failed-save established shell replaces only that named-family shell. Other illusion families retain their real rules; NEW where visual/voice overlays conflict, the most recently established operative covering shell supplies that channel, with no additive convincingness and older clocks continuing. An ended covering shell can expose a still-existing older different-family shell. Suppression, target death, expiry and applicable removal act independently per target and never reveal all other recipients or alter physical statistics.",
          "newChoices": "NEW six-recipient CHA/consent admission, independent hour-long shells, actual sampled/generic voice semantics, per-channel disbelief and independent dismissal/overlap.",
          "workedCases": [
            "IL5-01-A: Six legal recipients are selected; five accept and one unwilling creature succeeds CHA. Five distinct disguises appear for their original hour, with no seventh replacement. One leaves range afterward and retains its shell, but dropping a disguised carried item ends that item's overlay immediately.",
            "IL5-01-B: A shell resembles a heard captain's voice and silhouette. The recipient still cannot answer an unknown password or speak a language it does not know. A listener recognizes the voice overlay on an actual DC16Investigation success; this does not grant sight through a wall or expose the other five recipients."
          ],
          "questionId": "IL5-01",
          "originalQuestion": "Preserve UP TO6 targets appearing as others, expressly including VOICE and SILHOUETTE, Core Action/60ft/Instantaneous. Define valid creature targets, willingness/save, sight/line, independent disguise choices and finite duration/concentration. Establish dimensions and apparent equipment limits, moving-image behavior, sound production versus knowledge of a voice/language, inspection/touch/disbelief, and interaction with true sight and the reviewed Disguise Self/Distort Voice. Do not reduce the six-target/voice clauses to a generic visual disguise. It grants no actual form, hitbox, size, fit, carrying, anatomy, class ability, credentials or successful deception. Resolve one recipient losing the disguise, suppression, death, subsequent shapechange and recasts without refreshing unrelated resources or exposing all other targets.",
