        "completeEarlierRecordUnchanged": {
          "spellId": "spectral-army",
          "procedure": "KEEP five ghostly soldiers, all fake, 6d6 area psychic when attacked, Action, 60 feet, V/S/F and concentration up to one minute. NEW place exactly five distinct stationary images at five declared perceived points within range/line of effect. Each fits one 5-foot cube and depicts one humanoid-shaped spectral soldier chosen from appearances the caster actually knows. Images may occupy physically empty space without support, but not overlap one another or solid matter at creation. They are neither actual creatures nor objects with HP; occupied image space supplies no collision, cover, support, flanking body, corpse or inventory. They make only a simple repeated visible noninformational motion and no sound, attack, autonomous choice or sensory report. No movement/retarget command is added after casting.\n\nNEW each image is a specific legal apparent target for an ordinary attack roll, with apparent AC 10 solely to resolve that real attempt. After a genuine committed attack against it survives interruption and resolves its attack roll, hit or miss, that image is consumed and detonates exactly once. Mark it consumed before resolving the blast. The attacking action/ammunition/command costs remain real; no weapon-hit, damage-dealt, on-kill or creature-hit benefit arises against the image, even on an apparent hit. An attack canceled before its roll does not trigger it. An area damage effect without an actual attack roll targeting the image does not count as an attack for this trigger. Passing through, examination, speech and ordinary physical contradiction do not detonate it. The fake soldiers cannot attack one another.\n\nThe blast is a 10-foot-radius sphere centered on the consumed image's actual anchor, affecting every real creature in it with anchor line of effect, including the caster and allies. Each makes WIS; failure takes the shared rolled 6d6 psychic, success half rounded down. No object damage or other condition is added. This is explicitly magical psychic damage independent of believing the visual disguise: True Seeing or successful examination reveals the image without granting damage immunity. Actual psychic or broader applicable magical defenses still work. No blast can trigger another image, because it is not an attack roll and images are not its creature recipients. A single roll has one attacked image; a genuine multiattack can consume separate images only through separate real attack rolls. An already-queued attack against a now-consumed image fails against that missing target without a replacement image or refund unless its own actual source permits retargeting.\n\nDeliberate attacks by the caster, allies or an actually commanded companion are legal and retain their real action/ammunition and command/offense costs. There is no hidden enemy gate. The images themselves have no companion turn or command allowance; their automatic reactions to real attacks spend their finite discharge entitlement, not an invented creature attack. Maximum five detonations per cast, each consuming one of the actual five images. Disbelief alone neither consumes nor rearms an image. Suppression makes an affected image and its trigger unavailable; retained undischarged images can resume before original expiry, with no explosion for an attack while suppressed. Concentration loss, expiry, removal or voluntary concentration ending erases remaining images without detonating them. One active army per caster; a genuinely formed new army replaces the old without detonating it, while ordinary concentration commitment can already have ended the old one.",
          "workedCases": [
            "IN6-03-A: An ally spends a real ranged attack and ammunition against one image, rolls below apparent AC 10, and still triggers its single blast after that attack roll. Three creatures are inside the 10-foot sphere. A shared roll of 23 produces 23 on a failed WIS save or 11 on success, before each recipient's defenses. Four undischarged images remain; the blast does not trigger them.",
            "IN6-03-B: A True Seeing observer knows all five soldiers are images and can deliberately attack one. Identification prevents deception but not this explicitly separate psychic blast. Walking through another image does not detonate it. Ending concentration removes the four unused images quietly, with no corpse, loot, queued explosion or reusable discharge bank."
          ],
          "newChoices": "NEW five stationary attackable images, AC solely for real attempts, hit-or-miss trigger, 10-foot/WIS-half blasts, one discharge per image and deliberate allied triggering; no real creature or command budget.",
          "questionId": "IN6-03",
          "originalQuestion": "Preserve FIVE ghostly soldiers,ALL FAKE,and6d6 AREA PSYCHIC WHEN ATTACKED,Core Action/60ft/concentration up to1minute. Define creation positions,size,appearance,movement and whether these images have targetable image profiles rather than actual creature bodies. Specify what constitutes an attack and the trigger point for a hit/miss,area effects,allied/self attacks,illusions attacking each other and already-queued attacks. Give blast center,radius,recipients,save,packet count and finite per-image/whole-cast discharge limits; decide whether triggering consumes that image. Preserve five actual images and6d6 without permitting unbounded repeated discharge. They provide no corpses,loot,harvest,real soldiers,spellcasting or creature Actions merely from Summoning metadata. Reconcile disbelief,True Seeing,psychic immunity and the shared offensive-command rules if any actual commands or damage actions are authorized. No soul origin or afterlife facts follow from ghostly appearance.",
