        "completeEarlierRecordUnchanged": {
          "spellId": "programmed-illusion",
          "procedure": "KEEP Action, 60 feet, V/S/F and concentration up to one minute. NEW declare one fixed 20-foot cube whose center is perceived within range/line of effect, one trigger observation point inside that cube, one finite observable trigger condition and one predetermined performance lasting at most 30 seconds. The entire spell's 60-second maximum starts at casting resolution, not at triggering. The dormant image/sound is absent; the magical trigger remains a perceptible ongoing spell for an actually applicable detection/removal source, without being a creature or independent mind. Arming occurs after the cast resolves; a condition already genuinely true at that first observation may trigger immediately, but no event from before arming is replayed.\n\nThe trigger can observe ordinary visible shapes/motion or audible sounds within 30 feet of its fixed observation point through actual optical/acoustic paths. It has ordinary sight/hearing only, no darkvision, invisible detection, thoughts, alignment, secret names, creature-type diagnostic, knowledge of events through opaque walls or prediction. A simple conjunction of at most three such directly observable predicates can define the condition. A spoken password matches its declared audible pattern; a copied/imitated matching sound can satisfy it, and it does not identify the speaker's hidden legal identity. The condition is evaluated continuously as real eligible observations occur, not as free Perception checks against hidden facts. If an observation is genuinely unavailable or ambiguous, it cannot confirm the predicate; the caster receives no remote status or explanation.\n\nOn the first confirmed trigger, mark the one firing spent before beginning the recorded visual/audio performance. Simultaneous matching events still produce one firing. The performance stays inside the original cube and follows a fully predeclared finite sequence, using only known appearance/content or an actual literal sound sample. It can show moving creatures/objects and speech no louder than ordinary conversation through real acoustic paths; it creates no illumination, tangible heat, smell, support, cover, physical creature, damage, Action or spellcasting origin. It is not intelligent, adaptive dialogue and cannot answer an unrecorded question. The caster cannot amend its condition/script or move its anchor after casting. A new paid cast is required for a different program.\n\nEnd the performance at the earlier of its declared length or the original spell deadline. It does not loop, rearm, become permanent or get a fresh minute. LR-G07 examination/contradiction and True Seeing reveal its false sensory content for the actual observer but do not automatically stop other observers hearing/seeing it or dispel its trigger. Suppression makes affected sensory output and trigger observation unavailable. Events occurring wholly during suppression are missed, never queued. A persistent state still genuinely true when observation resumes may satisfy an unspent trigger then, with only original time remaining. Once fired, elapsed performance time continues through suppression; on resumption only the still-current remaining part can appear, with no replay. Concentration ending, removal or expiry cancels the dormant/fired program without executing an untriggered performance. One active Programmed Illusion per caster, with actual concentration commitment and replacement rules; no soldier, inventory, collectible recording object or future alarm service is created.",
          "workedCases": [
            "IN6-06-A: A program resolves at second 0 with a 30-second performance and a trigger when a visible person crosses the marked doorway. The first confirmed crossing occurs at second 50. The program can play only ten remaining seconds, ending at second 60; it does not receive a fresh 30-second performance or minute. Two simultaneous people crossing still trigger only that one firing.",
            "IN6-06-B: A password is spoken entirely while the trigger is suppressed and is therefore missed. Suppression later ends with 18 seconds left. A different declared persistent visual condition that is still truly observable may now trigger an unspent program, but the missed sound is not replayed. A copied voice can match the recorded sound without proving the speaker's identity or granting the caster a remote report."
          ],
          "newChoices": "NEW fixed cube/observation point, bounded ordinary trigger predicates, one finite scripted firing, no duration reset and exact suppression/missed-event behavior.",
          "questionId": "IN6-06",
          "originalQuestion": "Preserve an illusion TRIGGERED BY SPECIFIC CONDITIONS with actual Core Action/60ft/CONCENTRATION UP TO1MINUTE. Do not import a permanent sensor,ten-minute casting time,material price or another game's replay duration. Specify the image/sound geometry,allowed recorded performance,trigger detection range and actual observable information,initial arming and execution timestamps,number of firings and whether duration starts on casting or trigger. Resolve what happens if the trigger never occurs,concentration ends,condition becomes true while suppressed,or multiple targets/events occur together. A trigger cannot access secret thoughts,alignment,unknown names,events through walls or future information without an independently defined source. Reconcile disbelief,True Seeing and physical interaction; no creature/solid material,extra command budget or automatic damaging effect follows.",
          "fullSourceAndCurrentAccessRecord": {
