        },
        "IP14-SOURCE3-snapshots": {
          "id": "IP14-SOURCE3-snapshots",
          "completeText": "Choose all visible/perceived legal named targets, ordered lists, modes, centers, commands and appearances at commitment before hidden results. Recheck actual geometry and eligibility at resolution. Actual creature identity, current body/type/CR/HP, line of effect, cover and sensory gates control. A named-target spell requires perception and caster line of effect unless an exact exception is stated; ordinary area snapshots include unperceived bodies inside center line of effect. Hidden ineligibility spends an otherwise legal cast without furnishing a diagnostic. Enemy selection here means currently perceived creatures the caster affirmatively regards as hostile from available information, not a detector of true affiliation. Specific indiscriminate areas include allies. No flavor supplies real objects, extra bodies, terrain, damage, blindfolds or private memories.",
          "applicableSpellIds": [
